	(text "Pi console UART (GPIO14/15) to RS-232 on a 3-pin header. VCC from PI3.3: unpowered on boards without a Pi.\nHeader: TX - GND - RX, ground in the centre."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170 190 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1b59ce95-cc95-505e-a96a-64558941e4cf")
	)
	(text "IDEAL DIODE: LM74700-Q1 + AON7524 (30 V, 3.3 mOhm) blocks back-feed from the Pi's own USB-C.\nC24 (VCAP) connects to ANODE per the LM74700 datasheet; rated >= 25 V. 100 nF = 2.3 ms turn-on delay.\nBRING-UP: 3.3 mOhm is below TI's 8-20 mOhm window - scope the gate with the Pi idling for hunting."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170 22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7ed93d9e-9083-5565-90dd-07b359918997")
	)
	(text "RASPBERRY PI 40-PIN HEADER  (fit the Pi on ONE board only - nothing in hardware prevents three)\nFitted as a HAT-style 2x20 socket: the Pi sits below this board on standoffs, holes on the HAT pattern.\nPI_SDA/PI_SCL: the Pi has 1.8k pull-ups on GPIO2/3. Board-side pull-ups are DNP - more would\ndrop the effective pull-up too low. RESET_REQ is active-high: GPIO17 defaults to pull-down at boot."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c0d9ff92-cac0-566a-abf8-dce52b201073")
	)
	(text "TEST POINTS - Pi power, I2C, console UART (TTL side)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 23 261 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e8edb154-4078-53eb-a6a4-7e340829387c")
	)
	(text "HAT ID EEPROM on ID_SD / ID_SC (pins 27/28). Bridge JP to GND to write."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170 125 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ed0fc6be-aef1-51cb-97b8-166405a54d85")
	)
